<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagiellonian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jagiellonian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jagiellonian dynasty was a royal house that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and at times <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from the late fourteenth to the late sixteenth century. It began with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a>'s marriage to Jadwiga in 1386. Its long rule bound Poland and Lithuania together and led to the formation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> in 1569.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty.jpg" alt="Jagiellonian dynasty" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wereszczyński · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COA_Jagiellon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its dynastic union with Poland, begun at Krewo in 1385, produced the <b>Jagiellonian dynasty</b>, which at times ruled Poland, Lithuania, Bohemia and Hungary, and ultimately the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Polish nobles preferred to keep the <b>Jagiellonian dynasty</b> but to choose among its sons, believing that princes who had to earn the crown would be raised to be more capable.</blockquote><a href="/government/elective-monarchy">Elective monarchy · Strengths</a></li><li><blockquote>Sigismund II Augustus, last of the male <b>Jagiellons</b>, had no heir.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1385-1569">Kingdom of Poland (1385-1569)</a></li></ul></section>
